# Public keys allowed to JOIN a pairing session (`pair` passes this file to
# `upterm host --authorized-keys`). Having the session token is not enough:
# a participant also needs the private key matching one of these lines.
#
# One key per line, OpenSSH authorized_keys format; the trailing comment is
# free text, use it for "name@device" so it's obvious whose key it is:
#   ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... jan@macbook
#
# Add or remove people via a pull request. Hosts pick up changes by pulling
# and re-running the installer.
